<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-4c6b10543ff044928b0a00846e1f0bc3" title="sat-c2-u12-chronology.html qc2" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Working from time-stamped receipts and lobby-camera footage, detectives assembled a ____ of the night — who entered at 9:04, who slipped out at 9:40, when the alarm finally sounded.</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">chronology</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">chronicle</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">schedule</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">ledger</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Chronology means the order in which events actually happened — and fixing who entered at 9:04, who left at 9:40, and when the alarm sounded is precisely that: each event of the night set in its true place in time.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A chronicle is a written record kept as events unfold — set down while things happen, often year by year. The detectives are reconstructing the night after the fact, from receipts and footage; nothing was being recorded as it occurred.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A schedule lays out events still to come. This night is already over — the detectives are working out what did happen, not planning what will.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A ledger records accounts — sums received and sums paid. The receipts here serve as evidence of when things happened, not as entries in anyone&apos;s bookkeeping.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
